addition, the company provides debt cancellation products to its credit card customers through online and mobile channels; and healthcare payments and financing solutions under the CareCredit and Walgreens brands; payments and financing solutions in the apparel, specialty retail, outdoor, music, and luxury industries, such as American Eagle, Dick's Sporting Goods, Guitar Center, Pandora, Polaris, Suzuki, and Sweetwater. It offers its credit products through programs established with a group of national and regional retailers, local merchants, manufacturers, buying groups, industry associations, and healthcare service providers; and deposit products through various channels, such as digital and print. It serves digital, health and wellness, retail, home, auto, telecommunications, pet, outdoor, and other industries. The company was founded in 1932 and is headquartered in Stamford, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian D. Doubles | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $5.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20K people. Revenue per employee of $949K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Synchrony Financial is a large-cap financial services business with a $21.7B market cap on $19.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 15.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 21% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Synchrony Financial (NYSE:SYF) Showing Signs Of Renewed Strength?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/is-synchrony-financial-nysesyf-showing-signs-of-renewed-strength","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795632960.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SYF or AXP: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3035332/syf-or-axp-which-is-the-better-value-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-